# Phase 073 — Measure before optimizing: a benchmark harness with a checked-in baseline

## What changed

| File | Lines | What |
|---|---|---|
| `Cargo.toml` | +8 | Added the `rb-bench` binary target; it is a plain bin, not a `[[bench]]`, so `cargo test --all-targets` never runs the measuring code |
| `tests/bench/mod.rs` | +291 −29 | Four workloads (`fibonacci`, `primes`, `concat`, `lex`), reference-answer checks, a distinct `SizeTooLarge` refusal, a 60-second self-enforced budget shared across the no-argument run, table and `BENCH.md` rendering, an injectable output path, a checked wall-time cell parser, a manifest-root baseline path for tests, a platform-aware hardware probe, and an advisory `--compare` mode |
| `tests/bench/runner.rs` | +13 | The `rb-bench` entry point, outside the test gate path (landed in the first attempt) |
| `tests/bench_test.rs` | +210 −9 | Correctness, table, parsed-baseline, no-argument runner, numeric-limit, wall-time recording, baseline-parser, comparison-rendering, and edge-case tests that do run inside the gate |
| `tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` | +1 | Puts the in-flight `resume phase-073:` delivery prefix on the audit's delivery rule, so the delivery commit this phase produces is acknowledged by its subject rather than by a SHA that goes stale (landed in the first attempt) |
| `BENCH.md` | +8 −8 | The measured baseline from this landing machine: verified answers **and** wall times, plus the hardware note and the comparison contract |
| `.gitignore` | +2 −1 | The timing-ignore prose now names `BENCH.md` as the checked-in landing-machine baseline instead of claiming only answers are tracked |

The `Cargo.toml` binary target, `tests/bench/runner.rs` and
`tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs` landed in the first attempt and are already
in `HEAD`; the deltas above are the files this resumed run changes.

