# Redblue benchmarks

Generated by `cargo run --bin rb-bench`. This checked-in baseline records the verified answer and the wall time measured on the landing machine named below; the untracked `BENCH_TIMINGS.md` holds the record for the latest run. Only the answer is asserted by the test gate. The wall time is a debug-build reference: compare it on the same machine with `rb-bench --compare BENCH.md`, or compare the ratio between workloads across machines. Timings vary by machine and by run and are never asserted. The hardware line is best-effort; on a platform that does not expose a CPU model it says so explicitly.

